course: dictionary
lesson: 11657
title: Ascend: going up
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ascend is a formal word for go up, climb or rise. «The balloon ascended into the sky.» Ascended means went up, so you can swap in went up and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Ascend has special meanings too. «The young prince ascended the throne.» To ascend the throne means to become king. In maths, ascending order means from smallest to largest: 3, 7, 12, 20.
explain: Writers often choose ascend where a plain writer would say go up. Check the clues in the sentence: if climb or rise fits, ascend probably means the same thing.
fact: Ascend means to go up, climb or rise.
fact: «The balloon ascended into the sky» means the balloon went up into the sky.
fact: To ascend the throne means to become king or queen.
fact: In ascending order means arranged from the smallest to the largest, like 3, 7, 12, 20.
fact: Climbers ascend mountains, and air pressure falls as you ascend.
exercise: «The climbers began to ascend the steep mountain.» What does ascend mean here? | To shout loudly | To stop and have a rest | To go down | *To go up, climb
exercise: Put these numbers in ascending order. Which list is in ascending order? | 12, 20, 3, 7 | 20, 12, 7, 3 | *3, 7, 12, 20 | 7, 3, 20, 12
exercise: «The balloon ascended slowly.» Which word means the same as ascended? | Fell | *Rose | Stayed | Landed
test: «The new queen ascended the throne in the spring.» What does ascended the throne mean? | Sat down on a chair | Fell asleep | *Became queen | Left the castle
test: Which phrase means climb the stairs in formal language? | Sweep the stairs | Descend the stairs | Dance on the stairs | *Ascend the stairs
exam: Mia says, «Ascend means jump.» Which is the best meaning of ascend? | Shout very loudly | Sleep | Sink under water | *Go up, climb or rise
